body_text:
### Description
Checkstyle currently does not provide a check that detects duplicate conditional expressions across `if ... else if` chains.
### Proposed Check
`DuplicateConditionIfChainCheck`
The check should report `else if` conditional expressions whose AST structures are identical to any preceding condition in the same `if-else-if` chain.
### Violation Example
```java
class Test {
    void process(int value) {
        if (value > 0) {
            doSomething();
        } else if (value > 0) { // violation: duplicate condition
            doSomethingElse();
        } else if (value == 0) {
            doZero();
        }
    }
}
Expected violation:

Duplicate condition expression identical to the condition at line 3.

Non-Violation Example
java
class Test {
    void process(int value) {
        if (value > 10) {
            doHigh();
        } else if (value > 5) {
            doMedium();
        } else if (value > 0) {
            doLow();
        }
    }
}
What should NOT be flagged
Standalone if statements without else if branches.
Distinct conditional expressions in else if branches (e.g. x > 10 vs x > 5).
if statements nested inside the body of an else block (unless structured as an else if chain).
Expected Configuration
xml
<module name="Checker">
    <module name="TreeWalker">
        <module name="DuplicateConditionIfChain"/>
    </module>
</module>
Implementation Notes
Structural comparison on AST nodes (TokenTypes.EXPR) should be used rather than raw source code text comparison so formatting, whitespace, line breaks, and comments do not affect evaluation.
Middle branches of an if-else-if chain should be evaluated starting from the root LITERAL_IF node (ast.getParent().getType() != TokenTypes.LITERAL_ELSE).

