### Description
Java 9+ static factory methods like `Map.of(...)`, `Set.of(...)`, and `Map.ofEntries(...)` throw an `IllegalArgumentException` at runtime if passed duplicate keys or duplicate set elements. Checkstyle currently does not provide a check to detect duplicate key or element arguments passed to these factory methods at static analysis time.
### Proposed Check
`DuplicateMapOrSetKeyCheck`
The check should report key or element arguments passed to `Map.of`, `Set.of`, and `Map.ofEntries` whose AST structures match a preceding key or element argument in the same method call.
### Violation Example
```java
class Test {
    void process() {
        Map<String, Integer> map = Map.of(
            "key1", 1,
            "key2", 2,
            "key1", 3  // violation: duplicate key "key1"
        );
        Set<String> set = Set.of(
            "A",
            "B",
            "A"        // violation: duplicate element "A"
        );
        Map<String, Integer> entries = Map.ofEntries(
            Map.entry("k1", 1),
            Map.entry("k1", 2) // violation: duplicate entry key "k1"
        );
    }
}
Expected violations:

Duplicate key or element argument identical to the argument at line 4. Duplicate key or element argument identical to the argument at line 10. Duplicate key or element argument identical to the argument at line 16.

Non-Violation Example
java
class Test {
    void process() {
        Map<String, Integer> map = Map.of("a", 1, "b", 2);
        Set<String> set = Set.of("X", "Y", "Z");
    }
}
What should NOT be flagged
Non-factory method calls like custom map.of("a", "b").
Distinct keys or elements.
Expected Configuration
xml
<module name="Checker">
    <module name="TreeWalker">
        <module name="DuplicateMapOrSetKey"/>
    </module>
</module>
Implementation Notes
Subscribes to TokenTypes.METHOD_CALL.
Inspects target and method name (Map.of, Set.of, Map.ofEntries, Map.entry).
Structural AST equality (isAstEqual) is used so literal keys, enum constants, static fields, and expression keys are evaluated without noise from formatting or comments.

