from #18811 
I have read the Checkstyle documentation for [EmptyLineSeparator](https://checkstyle.org/checks/whitespace/emptylineseparator.html) and the [Google Java Style Guide 4.6.1](https://google.github.io/styleguide/javaguide.html#s4.6.1-vertical-whitespace) and 4.8.1 ([Enum classes](https://google.github.io/styleguide/javaguide.html#s4.8.1-enum-classes)).

The current `google_checks.xml` configuration does not include `ENUM_CONSTANT_DEF` in the `EmptyLineSeparator` check.

Google Java Style Guide 4.6.1 explicitly states that:

> "Blank lines between enum constants are covered in Section 4.8.1."

Section 4.8.1 further states:

> "After the comma that follows an enum constant, a line break is optional. Additional blank lines (usually just one) are also allowed."

**Expected:** `ENUM_CONSTANT_DEF` should be included in the `EmptyLineSeparator` configuration so that blank-line handling between enum constants follows the Google Java Style Guide.

For example:

```java
enum Answer {
  YES,

  NO,
  MAYBE
}
```
should be handled according to the enum-specific formatting rules.

Adding `ENUM_CONSTANT_DEF` to `google_checks.xml` would make the Checkstyle Google configuration explicitly account for enum constants instead of relying on the general class-member handling.

**Expected configuration change:**
```xml
<module name="EmptyLineSeparator">
    ...
    <property name="tokens"
              value="..., ENUM_CONSTANT_DEF"/>
</module>
```

This would align the Google Checkstyle configuration with the enum-specific rules documented in the Google Java Style Guide.

### Google Formatter Example
```
$ java -jar google-java-format-1.37.0-all-deps.jar Test.java > FormattedCode.java
$ diff -Naru Test.java FormattedCode.java
--- Test.java   2026-10-02 00:25:31.386072400 +0530
+++ FormattedCode.java  2026-10-02 00:28:24.755438200 +0530
@@ -1,26 +1,18 @@
- public class Test {
+public class Test {

   public enum Check {
-
     FIRST,
     SECOND,

     THIRD,

-
     FOURTH,

-
     SPECIAL(100) {
       @Override
-      public String describe() {
-
-      }
+      public String describe() {}
     },

-
-
-
     NORMAL(200) {
       @Override
       public String describe() {
@@ -28,4 +20,4 @@
       }
     };
   }
-}
\ No newline at end of file
+}
```

