I have read the check documentation: https://checkstyle.org/checks/misc/indentation.html

Reproduced with the latest release, Checkstyle 14.3.0, downloaded from its GitHub release. The same behavior is present on master `229c44f8a17b8ec892469a4ff7eeb46300794d89`. Both Java examples compile successfully.

```sh
javac -encoding UTF-8 AnnotationArrayExample.java
# Successful compilation, no output

cat annotation-indentation.xml
```

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN" "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">
<module name="Checker">
  <module name="TreeWalker">
    <module name="Indentation">
      <property name="arrayInitIndent" value="0"/>
      <property name="basicOffset" value="2"/>
      <property name="lineWrappingIndentation" value="0"/>
    </module>
  </module>
</module>
```

```sh
cat AnnotationArrayExample.java
```

```java
@𝒜({ "first",
     "second"})
class AnnotationArrayExample {
}

@𝒜({ "first",
    "second"})
class IncorrectAnnotationArray {
}

@Α({ "first",
     "second"})
class BmpAnnotationArray {
}

@interface 𝒜 {
  String[] value();
}

@interface Α {
  String[] value();
}
```

```sh
java -Duser.language=en -Duser.country=US -jar checkstyle-14.3.0-all.jar -c annotation-indentation.xml AnnotationArrayExample.java
Starting audit...
[ERROR] AnnotationArrayExample.java:2:6: 'annotation array initialization' child has incorrect indentation level 5, expected level should be one of the following: 0, 3, 4. [Indentation]
Audit done.
Checkstyle ends with 1 errors.
```

Expected behavior:

The first annotation array is correctly aligned at code-point column 5 and should pass, as does the BMP Greek annotation control at line 12. The second annotation array at line 7 has only four spaces and should report expected levels 0, 3 and 5. Current Checkstyle instead rejects the correctly aligned line 2 and accepts the incorrectly aligned line 7.

Investigation:

`AnnotationArrayInitHandler.getNextFirstNonBlankOnLineAfter` uses AST code-point columns to index a UTF-16 String. The supplementary annotation identifier occupies two UTF-16 code units, shifting the computed alignment one position. Using code points for the line scan fixes the mismatch. This is the annotation-array portion of #10924, split into a focused issue as requested in https://github.com/checkstyle/checkstyle/issues/10924#issuecomment-5785685046.

A focused fix and regression tests are prepared locally. Please approve this bug for a separate contribution.

