I have read the [[RedundantThis documentation](https://checkstyle.org/checks/coding/redundantthis.html)](https://checkstyle.org/checks/coding/redundantthis.html).

I downloaded Checkstyle 14.4.0 and reproduced the issue with the following minimal example.

### Configuration

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC
  "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
  "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">
<module name="Checker">
  <module name="TreeWalker">
    <module name="RedundantThis"/>
  </module>
</module>
```

### Test case

```java
import java.util.function.BiConsumer;
import java.util.function.Consumer;

public class TestLambda {
    private int value;
    private String text;

    public void example() {
        Consumer<Integer> c1 = value -> {
            this.value = value;
        };

        Consumer<Integer> c2 = (Integer value) -> {
            this.value = value;
        };

        BiConsumer<Integer, String> c3 = (value, text) -> {
            this.value = value;
            this.text = text;
        };

        Consumer<Integer> c4 = value -> this.value = value;
    }
}
```

### Actual behavior

Checkstyle reports all five `this.` qualifications as redundant:

```text
[ERROR] TestLambda.java:11:13: Redundant "this", field 'value' can be accessed directly. [RedundantThis]
[ERROR] TestLambda.java:16:13: Redundant "this", field 'value' can be accessed directly. [RedundantThis]
[ERROR] TestLambda.java:21:13: Redundant "this", field 'value' can be accessed directly. [RedundantThis]
[ERROR] TestLambda.java:22:13: Redundant "this", field 'text' can be accessed directly. [RedundantThis]
[ERROR] TestLambda.java:26:41: Redundant "this", field 'value' can be accessed directly. [RedundantThis]
```

### Expected behavior

**0 violations.**

All five `this.` qualifications are required because the instance fields are shadowed by lambda parameters with the same names.

For example:

```java
Consumer<Integer> c1 = value -> {
    this.value = value;
};
```

cannot safely be changed to:

```java
Consumer<Integer> c1 = value -> {
    value = value;
};
```

The latter assigns the lambda parameter to itself and no longer updates the instance field.

The same issue occurs with parenthesized/typed lambda parameters, multiple lambda parameters, and expression-body lambdas.

### Root cause

`RedundantThisCheck` does not appear to track lambda parameters as local variables.

In particular:

- `TokenTypes.LAMBDA` is not included in the accepted tokens.
- Lambda parameters are therefore not added to `scopeStack`.
- As a result, `isShadowedByLocalName(name)` does not recognize a lambda parameter as shadowing a field.

This causes `RedundantThisCheck` to incorrectly report required `this.` qualifications inside lambda bodies.

### Suggested fix

Lambda parameters should be added to the appropriate scope when entering a `LAMBDA` node and removed when leaving it, so that field shadowing is handled consistently with method and other local scopes.

The regression test should cover at least:

- `value -> ...`
- `(Integer value) -> ...`
- `(value, text) -> ...`
- expression-body lambdas

