Hi there 👋 ,
I'm currently using v4.6.5

Given the following example schema

```ts
z.object({
  foo: z.int().min(5),
  bar: z.int().min(1)
})
```

If you want to make sure that `bar` must be smaller than `foo` using [`.superRefine()`](https://zod.dev/api#superrefine) does the job

```ts
  schema.superRefine((data, ctx) => {
    const { foo, bar } = data;

    if (bar > foo) {
      ctx.addIssue({
        code: "too_big",
        message: `There is a maximum of ${foo - 1}.`,
        path: ["bar"],
      });
    }
  });
```

but I think in my case using [`.refine()`](https://zod.dev/api#refine) is "good enough" (requires less manual effort)

```ts
  schema.refine(
    ({ foo, bar }) => bar < foo,
    {
      error: ({ input }) => {
        const { foo } = input; // input is unknown, not fully typed

        return `There is a maximum of ${foo - 1}.`
      },
      path: ["bar"],
    },
  )
```

The problem here is that the `issue` parameter passed to the `error` function does not provide types for the `input` field. `input` is of type `unknown` although I would expect the type to be `z.infer<typeof schema>`.

Is this expected behavior...?

Thanks 😄

