body_text:
We have an API where Zod is used for type checking. 
Here is an example (shorter) of the schema for the POST endpoint:

```typescript
z.object({
  a: z.string().default('a'),
  b: z.string().default('b'),
});
```

We also have a PATCH endpoint. We derive the schema from the Post schema:

```typescript
z.object({
  a: z.string().default('a'),
  b: z.string().default('b'),
}).partial();
```

Passing in the following to the PATCH endpoint:
```json
{
    "b": "ddd",
}
```

In Zod 3, the parsed value would be:
```json
{
    "b": "ddd"
}
```

In Zod 4:
```json
{
    "a": "a",
    "b": "ddd"
}
```
