`z.fromJSONSchema()` in Zod 4.5.0 silently accepts JSON Schema 2020-12 `$dynamicRef` as metadata. This can omit validation of a recursively referenced child.

```ts
import { z } from "zod";

const schema = {
  $schema: "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema" as const,
  $ref: "#/$defs/node",
  $defs: {
    node: {
      $dynamicAnchor: "node",
      type: "object" as const,
      required: ["value"],
      properties: {
        value: { type: "number" as const },
        child: { $dynamicRef: "#node" },
      },
    },
  },
};

const parsed = z.fromJSONSchema(schema).safeParse({
  value: 1,
  child: { value: "not a number" },
});
console.log(parsed.success); // true
```

Expected: either enforce the dynamic reference and reject this value, or throw during conversion with `$dynamicRef is not supported`, consistent with other unsupported import features. Actual: conversion succeeds and the invalid child passes.

Proposed narrow approach: extend the [existing unsupported-feature check](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/blob/v4.5.0/packages/zod/src/v4/classic/from-json-schema.ts#L199), before `$ref` resolution:

```ts
if (ctx.version === "draft-2020-12" && schema.$dynamicRef !== undefined) {
  throw new Error("$dynamicRef is not supported");
}
```

This uses the existing schema conversion traversal rather than scanning arbitrary JSON. Static `$ref`, old-draft unknown annotations, and data objects under `default` or `examples` should retain their behavior. This is a proposal to reject an unsupported feature, not an implementation of dynamic-reference resolution.

