{"repository": "denoland/deno", "task_candidate_id": 3569, "repository_id": 68, "issue_number": 36704, "github_issue_id": 5266287816, "html_url": "https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/36704", "created_at": "2026-08-27T10:00:50+00:00", "author_association": "NONE", "title": "WebSocket ignores http2:false on the client's HttpClient — always offers h2 in ALPN, breaks upgrades against Traefik/nginx/Caddy", "body_text": "## Summary

`new WebSocket(url, { client: Deno.createHttpClient({ http2: false }) })` does not force `http/1.1` in the TLS ALPN offer. Every WebSocket connection still advertises `h2` in ALPN. Against any server that offers `h2` in ALPN (Traefik, Caddy default, most modern ingresses), the WS handshake fails at the h2 stream layer because `Deno.upgradeWebSocket`-style HTTP/1.1 `Upgrade: websocket` is not valid inside an HTTP/2 stream.

The `http2: false` flag works for `fetch()`: it removes `h2` from the ALPN offer and the request goes over `http/1.1`. Same flag is silently ignored on `new WebSocket()`.

## Reproduction

Any Traefik or nginx or Caddy configured to offer `h2, http/1.1` on the wss:// endpoint reproduces. Minimal client:

```ts
const url = "wss://<host-with-h2-alpn>/";

async function probe(label: string, opts: WebSocketInit) {
  console.log(`--- ${label} ---`);
  const ws = new WebSocket(url, opts);
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
    ws.onopen = () => { console.log(`  open`); ws.close(); resolve(); };
    ws.onerror = (e) =>
      console.log(`  error: ${(e as ErrorEvent).message}`);
    ws.onclose = (e) => {
      const ce = e as CloseEvent;
      console.log(`  close code=${ce.code} reason=${ce.reason || "(empty)"}`);
      resolve();
    };
    setTimeout(() => resolve(), 5000);
  });
}
type WebSocketInit = any;

await probe("no client", {});
await probe("http2:false client", {
  client: Deno.createHttpClient({ http2: false }),
});
await probe("default client", {
  client: Deno.createHttpClient({}),
});
```

Observed on Deno 2.9.5 (aarch64-apple-darwin), same behavior on 2.8.3 embedded in `deno compile` binaries:

```
--- no client ---
  error: NetworkError: failed to connect to WebSocket:
    HTTP/2 not supported by this client
--- http2:false client ---
  error: NetworkError: failed to connect to WebSocket:
    stream error received: unspecific protocol error detected
--- default client ---
  error: NetworkError: failed to connect to WebSocket:
    stream error received: unspecific protocol error detected
```

Compare with `fetch(url.replace("wss://", "https://"), { client: Deno.createHttpClient({ http2: false }) })` against the same endpoint — it correctly negotiates `http/1.1` and succeeds.

## Expected

Setting `http2: false` on the `HttpClient` passed to `new WebSocket(url, { client })` should remove `h2` from the ALPN offer, matching `fetch()` behaviour. The upgrade then goes over `http/1.1` and succeeds.

Alternatively, a per-WebSocket ALPN override — `new WebSocket(url, { client, alpnProtocols: ["http/1.1"] })` — would be enough. Today there is no way to force `http/1.1` for a WebSocket at all.

## Impact

Any Deno client speaking WebSocket to a Traefik/nginx/Caddy/Envoy that offers `h2` in ALPN fails. Downstream this blocked worker enrollment in the swamp automation platform (swamp-club/swamp#2260, swamp-club Lab #1843). The workaround the community has landed on is placing an h1.1-only reverse proxy in front, but that is deployment infrastructure, not a client fix.

Filed on behalf of an active production workload. Happy to test any patch on our repro.

## Reference

