body_text:
Currently, only handler that `deno serve` command can accept is default export, so running `Deno.serve()` will result in an error.

This proposal would allow a handler for `Deno.serve()` to be accepted in addition to the default export, allowing users to use serve command without changing existing code.

A advantage of using serve command is that `--parallel` flag allows for parallel processing.

ex.)

```ts
// server.ts

// All of following result in same behavior.
export default {
    fetch() {
        return new Response("hello");
    }
};

Deno.serve(() => {
    return new Response("hello");
});

// Need to consider whether to incorporate or disregard options.
Deno.serve({
    hostname: "192.168.0.123",
    port: 9876
}, () => {
    return new Response("hello");
});
```

```sh
deno serve ./server.ts
```

