body_text:
Version: Deno 2.9.7

It seems that `worker_threads` workers can be unreffed in `deno`, but web workers cannot. This is extremely necessary functionality  libraries that want to ship a portable API based on web workers, so I'd like to advocate for support.

`bun` supports unreffing web workers, and so does `node`'s flagged implementation. This also interacts with https://github.com/denoland/deno/issues/36993

Repro:

```js
// test.js
const worker = new Worker(
  URL.createObjectURL(
    new Blob(
      [`globalThis.addEventListener("message", (e) => { globalThis.postMessage("Received: " + e.data); });`],
      { type: "text/javascript" },
    ),
  ),
  { type: "module" },
);
worker.addEventListener("message", (e) => {
  console.log(e.data);
  globalThis.process?.unref?.(worker);
});
worker.postMessage("hi");
```

```shell
bun run -- ./test.js                     # succeeds and exits
node --experimental-web-worker ./test.js # succeeds and exits
deno run ./test.js                       # hangs
````

