body_text:
## Problem

When a web app has its own `index.html`, `dx` writes the `[web.app] title` of `Dioxus.toml` into the page in the wrong way.

- **A `<title>` already written in `index.html` gets the configured title appended to it.** `<title>My App</title>` with `title = "My App"` becomes `<title>My AppMy App</title>`. When no title is configured, the default is appended instead: `<title>My Appdioxus | ⛺</title>`.
- **An `index.html` without `<title>` gets no title at all.** The configured title is dropped, and nothing says so.

Seen with dx 0.7.9. The same code is on `main` (7a81739): `packages/cli/src/build/web.rs`, `prepare_html`:

```rust
let title = self.config.web.app.title.clone();
Self::replace_or_insert_before("{app_title}", "</title", &title, &mut html);
```

When the placeholder is absent, `replace_or_insert_before` inserts the title just before `</title`, so it lands after any existing text. When there is no `</title` either, it does nothing.

## Steps to reproduce

1. In a web crate, add an `index.html` whose `<head>` contains `<title>My App</title>`.
2. Set `[web.app] title = "My App"` in `Dioxus.toml`, or leave it unset.
3. Run `dx build --platform web`.
4. Open `target/dx/<crate>/debug/web/public/index.html`. The title is `My AppMy App`, or `My Appdioxus | ⛺` when the title is unset.
5. Remove the `<title>` element and build again. The page has no `<title>`.

Workaround today: write `<title></title>` or `<title>{app_title}</title>` in `index.html`.

## Expected behavior

- `{app_title}` is replaced, as today.
- An empty `<title>` is filled with the configured title.
- A non-empty `<title>` written in `index.html` is kept as written.
- With no `<title>` at all, `<title>…</title>` is added before `</head>`.

Keeping a hand-written title rather than overwriting it with `[web.app] title` is a choice: the patch below takes the HTML author's side, because the default title would otherwise replace every custom one. If you would rather have `Dioxus.toml` win when a title is set explicitly, that is your call. Either way, both titles should not be concatenated.

## Patch

Against `main` 7a81739, tests written first.

How it was checked: `inject_title` and the `build::web::tests` module were compiled on their own with `rustc --test`. On the current behaviour, 3 of the 5 tests fail: `empty_title_is_filled`, `title_written_in_index_html_is_kept` and `missing_title_is_added_to_head`. With the patch, all 5 pass. `rustfmt --check` is clean on the file. I could not run `cargo test -p dioxus-cli` on the whole crate on this machine, so please let CI confirm that it builds.

```diff
diff --git a/packages/cli/src/build/web.rs b/packages/cli/src/build/web.rs
index 677ee7b..c150d22 100644
--- a/packages/cli/src/build/web.rs
+++ b/packages/cli/src/build/web.rs
@@ -405,7 +405,7 @@ __wbg_init({{module_or_path: "/{}/{wasm_path}"}}).then((wasm) => {{
         self.replace_template_placeholders(&mut html, wasm_path, js_path);

         let title = self.config.web.app.title.clone();
-        Self::replace_or_insert_before("{app_title}", "</title", &title, &mut html);
+        inject_title(&title, &mut html);

         Ok(html)
     }
@@ -608,6 +608,31 @@ __wbg_init({{module_or_path: "/{}/{wasm_path}"}}).then((wasm) => {{
     }
 }

+/// Put the app title in the page: replace `{app_title}`, fill an empty
+/// `<title>`, or add a `<title>` to `<head>`. A title already written in
+/// index.html is kept.
+fn inject_title(title: &str, html: &mut String) {
+    if html.contains("{app_title}") {
+        *html = html.replace("{app_title}", title);
+        return;
+    }
+    if let Some(open) = html.find("<title") {
+        let Some(start) = html[open..].find('>').map(|i| open + i + 1) else {
+            return;
+        };
+        let Some(end) = html[start..].find("</title").map(|i| start + i) else {
+            return;
+        };
+        if html[start..end].trim().is_empty() {
+            html.replace_range(start..end, title);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+    if let Some(head_end) = html.find("</head") {
+        html.insert_str(head_end, &format!("<title>{title}</title>"));
+    }
+}
+
 #[cfg(test)]
 mod tests {
     #[test]
@@ -618,4 +643,46 @@ mod tests {
         assert!(!DEV_INDEX.contains("fonts.googleapis.com"));
         assert!(!DEV_LOADING.contains("fonts.googleapis.com"));
     }
+
+    fn titled(html: &str) -> String {
+        let mut html = html.to_string();
+        super::inject_title("My App", &mut html);
+        html
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn title_placeholder_is_replaced() {
+        assert_eq!(
+            titled("<head><title>{app_title}</title></head>"),
+            "<head><title>My App</title></head>"
+        );
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn empty_title_is_filled() {
+        assert_eq!(
+            titled("<head><title></title></head>"),
+            "<head><title>My App</title></head>"
+        );
+        assert_eq!(
+            titled("<head><title lang=\"en\">  </title></head>"),
+            "<head><title lang=\"en\">My App</title></head>"
+        );
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn title_written_in_index_html_is_kept() {
+        assert_eq!(
+            titled("<head><title>Custom</title></head>"),
+            "<head><title>Custom</title></head>"
+        );
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn missing_title_is_added_to_head() {
+        assert_eq!(
+            titled("<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"></head>"),
+            "<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>My App</title></head>"
+        );
+    }
 }
```

## Environment

- dx 0.7.9 (bfcc111), and `main` 7a81739
- macOS 26 (Darwin 25.3), aarch64

