body_text:
ECJ reports a type mismatch for a lambda body whose type is captured, while the target type of the whole expression accepts it.

```java
import java.util.*;
public class T1 {
    static List<Class<?>> f(Optional<Integer> o, Class<?>[] a) {
        return o.map(n -> List.of(Arrays.copyOf(a, n))).orElse(List.of());
    }
}
```

```
T1.java (at line 4)
	return o.map(n -> List.of(Arrays.copyOf(a, n))).orElse(List.of());
	       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Type mismatch: cannot convert from List<Class<capture#1-of ?>> to List<Class<?>>
```

javac infers `R := List<Class<?>>` for `Optional.map`. ECJ seems to use the type of the lambda body, `List<Class<capture#1-of ?>>`, as the bound of `R` and then cannot convert it to the target type.

I found it by compiling the JDK 25 sources with ECJ: ``java.base/java/lang/invoke/MethodHandles.java:6545`` is one of the few errors ECJ reports on code that javac builds.

### Environment

- ECJ `org.eclipse.jdt.core.compiler.batch_3.46.100.v20260826-1225` (Eclipse 2026-09), `-21`
- JustJ OpenJDK 25.0.4
- javac 25 accepts the code (`--release 21`)

