The cycle `AbstractFuture extends AbstractFutureState` with `AbstractFutureState` importing from `AbstractFuture` is part of it. My guess (not checked in the compiler code): resolving the enum constant of the annotation forces the resolution of member types while the hierarchy of `AbstractFutureState` is still being connected (triggered by the static import loading `AbstractFuture`), and the member types of `AbstractFutureState` are read before they are complete, so `AtomicHelper` is not found.

With the real Guava sources, the same problem gives 10 errors in `AbstractFutureState.java` (javac compiles it).

I could not find an existing issue.

This report was prepared with the help of Claude (Anthropic); the reproducer was checked with javac and ECJ.
